### Topic 51 - Caching with Redis
### Use with the VS Code "REST Client" extension: click "Send Request" above each request.
### Watch the X-Response-Time-Ms header and the application log!

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080

### 1) First read of product 1 -> cache MISS (about 2000 ms)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/products/1

### 2) Same request again -> cache HIT (a few ms)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/products/1

### 3) Search by category -> first time slow, then fast
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/products?category=laptops

### 4) Search term shorter than 3 chars -> condition is false -> NEVER cached (always slow)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/products?category=ph

### 5) How many REAL database hits so far?
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/products/stats

### 6) Update a price -> @CachePut refreshes "products::1", search lists are evicted
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/products/1/price
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "price": 999.00
}

### 7) Read product 1 again -> still FAST and shows the NEW price
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/products/1

### 8) Create a product -> it is put into the cache immediately
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/products
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Lenovo ThinkPad X1",
  "category": "laptops",
  "price": 1499.00
}

### 9) Delete a product -> @CacheEvict removes it from the cache
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/products/5

### 10) Look inside the caches
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/caches

### 11) Clear one cache
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/caches/products

### 12) Clear all caches
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/caches
